 @_qwe_fk_1700  The 3080 had 85% of the CUDA Cores of the 3090. As such the gap in performance between the two cards was small.

This isn't last gen. Anyone expecting the 4080 16GB to get anywhere near the 4090's performance is delusional. The 4090 has 6656 more CUDA cores. The 12GB "4080" is even worse. The 4090 has 8704 more CUDA cores. That's more CUDA cores than the 12GB model has. It has 7680.

If you use the RTX 20 and 30 series as a guide. The RTX 4080 16GB should be a 4070 and the 12GB 4080 should be a 4060Ti.

